Remarks
To create a new DataRow, you must use the NewRow method to return a new object. Such an object is automatically configured according to the schema defined for the DataTable through its collection of DataColumn objects. After creating a new row and setting the values for each column in the row, add the row to the DataRowCollection using the Add
method.
Each DataRow in the collection represents a row of data in the table. To commit a change to the value of a column in the row, you must invoke the AcceptChanges method.

